    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "531045",
        "date_added": "2026-11-22 11:34:19",
        "twitter_handle": null,
        "display_name": null,
        "comment": "FluxEngine loader dhlib.dll (Delphi DLL, export InitModule), compiled 2026-11-17, carved byte-for-byte from the hex blob in the a3x 4fc99727 (never on disk). Same AES master key and Cloudflare API token as the Sep/Oct 2026 builds (dc60f22f et al., compared by hash). Gets UrlSource from a Cloudflare TXT record (lurlsource.\u003czone\u003e), downloads d3dx9_43.bin from the panel (/api/source-file.php), decrypts it and hollows a suspended attrib.exe (CFG off). The panel d3dx9_43.bin, fetched 2026-11-22, decrypts with this build key to payload c2225d92.\n\nChain (static analysis): DOC-*.vbs -\u003e regsvr32 /i:%TEMP%\\t\u003cdigits\u003e.sct scrobj.dll (recon scriptlet) -\u003e installer scriptlet -\u003e C:\\\u003c8 letters\u003e\\ with signed AutoIt3 (renamed) + compiled script -\u003e in-memory dhlib.dll (InitModule) -\u003e AES container from the operator panel -\u003e hollowed attrib.exe -\u003e FluxEngine client. C2 address is read from a DNS TXT record through the Cloudflare API with an embedded token.\nRules, IOCs: https://github.com/harperjohnsai/detections/tree/main/iocs/2026-11-fluxengine\nHarper Johns, security researcher\nMore research: youtube.com/@HarperJohnsAI"
      }
    ],
